<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco Serrano, 1st Duke of la Torre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1810">1810</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco Serrano was a Spanish general and politician who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution-spain">Glorious Revolution</a> of September 1868 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-prim">Juan Prim</a> and Admiral Topete, driving Isabella II into exile. He served as regent until Amadeo I arrived in 1871, and after the Pavía coup of January 1874 he headed the executive of the First Republic until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> restoration that December.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-serrano-1st-duke-of-la-torre.jpg" alt="Francisco Serrano, 1st Duke of la Torre" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nadar%27s_photo_of_Serrano_(Retouched).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
